== (c) recursion convention for +: textbook Q4,Q5 (right) versus Q4L,Q5L (left), both with Ind
  Q4 in T_left    lines  11  written  33  overhead 213.8 bits per use
  Q5 in T_left    lines  22  written  98  overhead 593.4 bits per use
  Q4L in T_right  lines  11  written  33  overhead 213.8 bits per use
  Q5L in T_right  lines  21  written  89  overhead 545.1 bits per use
  (Q + Ind has 8 axioms; a citation costs log2(10)+log2(8) bits.)
  T_right beats T_left iff  r4*213.8 + r5*593.4 > l4*213.8 + l5*545.1, with r_i, l_i the usage rates of
  Q_i and of the left variants: the posterior adopts the convention the data use.

== (b) ZF: checked derivations between schema forms (schematic in P(u) / R(x,y))
  SepJ from ReplJ        lines  36  written 207  K 19  overhead 1209.3 bits;  template |SepJ| = 16 symbols (72 bits)
  Found from EInd        lines  21  written 138  K  0  overhead  758.1 bits;  template |Found| = 24 symbols (109 bits)
  ReplK from Coll        lines  15  written 108  K 12  overhead  574.1 bits;  template |ReplK| = 41 symbols (185 bits)
  ReplJ from Coll+SepJ   lines  43  written 237  K 21  overhead 1432.0 bits;  template |ReplJ| = 37 symbols (167 bits)
  not computed (long; see notes): Coll from Repl (needs ranks and Power Set), EInd from Found (needs
  transitive closures, hence Infinity and Replacement).
  Overheads are upper bounds on the true minimum (shortest derivations were not searched).

