break-even under the naive code (T_Ind beats T_CVI iff p_CVI/p_Ind < overhead(Ind|T_CVI)/overhead(CVI|T_Ind)):
  |phi|=5: 0.671  |phi|=10: 0.776  |phi|=20: 0.900  |phi|=40: 1.052

== base axioms cited by each derivation (the base theory over which the equivalences are proved)
  Ind <- CVI (A)       cites ['CVI', 'Dlt', 'Q3', 'Q4', 'Q5']
  CVI <- Ind (B)       cites ['Dlt', 'Ind', 'Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4', 'Q5']
  LNP <- CVI(~) (C1)   cites ['CVI']
  CVI <- LNP(~) (C2)   cites ['LNP']
  Q4 <- left+Ind       cites ['Ind', 'Q4L', 'Q5L']
  Q5 <- left+Ind       cites ['Ind', 'Q4L', 'Q5L']
  Q4L <- right+Ind     cites ['Ind', 'Q4', 'Q5']
  Q5L <- right+Ind     cites ['Ind', 'Q4', 'Q5']
